WEBVTT

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:15.640
My right hand holds a bowl of gold,

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:20.180
And my left holds one of silver.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:24.720
Never one without the other,

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:37.800
Two unseen bowls for each of us.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:46.210
The golden one is filled with joy,

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:53.550
shining warmly.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:58.350
Since we met, my golden bowl

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:05.360
cannot hold all my happiness and love.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:15.500
Golden joy, silver sadness,

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:22.850
I would leave my past behind...

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:27.580
For you, for the sake of love,

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:34.520
I would empty the bowls of my past.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.370
Hey, Nanako...

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:04.400
After swim class, let's get something to eat at the Road House, and then go see "Love Awakening!"

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.000
Hmm...

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:09.420
Come on! It's been so long since we've just gone out and <i>done</i> something.

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:10.360
Hmm...

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:15.160
I'll consider it, OK?

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:18.060
Seriously, give it some thought.

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:24.730
<i>My dear brother....</i>

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:28.550
<i>It has been over two weeks now since Saint-Juste-sama passed away.</i>

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:34.940
<i>Additionally, the Sorority members learned of what Miya-sama said; now that whole tradition has come to an end.</i>

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:42.470
<i>And now, finally, summer vacation has arrived at Seiran Academy.</i>

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:48.990
<i>I am doing well, dear brother.</i>

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:54.390
<i>I hope to be able to write you a letter any day now...</i>

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:06.670
<b>36. Light of the Fireflies, Ablaze with Passion...</b>

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:11.210
Have a seat here.

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:19.810
Orihara-san, the doctor would like to take a look at how the affected area is progressing.

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:21.560
Please undress.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:22.960
Yes, ma'am.

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:30.630
Orihara-san, please remove everything.

00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:31.910
Oh, right....

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:46.280
Hmm... I suppose you'll be pretty busy during the summer break, with your club activities?

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:47.820
No, not really....

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:53.830
So you can come in every other week then, right?

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:57.980
You only got out of the hospital a year ago, and it would be best to run some more detailed tests.

00:03:58.580 --> 00:04:01.660
So then... I'm not going to make it, am I?

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:04.410
Oh, now, I didn't say anything like that!

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:07.560
Just give it to me straight! I want to know!

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:09.170
You have nothing to worry about.

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:14.330
If I thought it might be serious, I'd have you back in the hospital until we knew for certain.

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:18.180
Believe me!

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:20.380
Excuse me!

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:22.120
Hey! Orihara-kun!

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:46.820
Yeah, that Larry Duncan is pretty good!

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:50.240
How about we hop over to the Roxy for a quick drink?

00:04:52.010 --> 00:04:53.820
The flowers....

00:04:53.820 --> 00:04:54.890
Huh?

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:56.700
I don't want the flowers to dry out....

00:04:57.680 --> 00:04:59.690
Nanako! Where are you going?

00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:03.420
Nanako...

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:19.200
Hey, Nanako! There's somebody there!

00:05:19.730 --> 00:05:20.470
Eh?

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:22.080
Up there! See?

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:23.960
What...?

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:25.230
Where?

00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:27.110
Up on the overpass.

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:28.110
There!

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:30.460
They've been just sitting there for a while now.

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:50.260
<i>My dear brother, Kaoru-no-Kimi was....</i>

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:04.970
<i>Dear brother... Kaoru-no-Kimi was crying....</i>

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:09.480
<i>It was as though all her deepest sorrows were finally risen to the surface....</i>

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:12.690
<i>As if she were forced against her will by her own despair....</i>

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:17.130
<i>Indeed, my brother...</i>

00:06:17.130 --> 00:06:22.950
<i>...I saw then that there was another apart from myself who could not come to terms with Saint-Juste-sama's death....</i>

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:27.490
<i>One for whom the pain of sorrow runs deeper than I could ever know....</i>

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:31.180
<i>One whose grief is so strong... it is tearing her apart....</i>

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:33.740
<i>Kaoru-no-Kimi...</i>

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:40.640
<i>Kaoru-no-Kimi, whom I had always thought to be so strong, so unshakable...</i>

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:42.920
<i>That Kaoru-no-Kimi is crying now...</i>

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:45.770
<i>Rei....</i>

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:47.730
<i>Rei!</i>

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:49.810
<i>Rei....</i>

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:56.960
<i>Why are people born into this world?</i>

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:03.280
<i>And why do they even bother to go on living?</i>

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:06.620
<i>They're all going to die someday, anyway!</i>

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:18.480
Hello, Joutou University, Department of Humanities and Cultural Studies....

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:21.670
Yes, come in.

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:26.820
There was a call for you while you were out earlier, Professor.

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:31.300
The caller was a Mr. Henmi Takehiko, from the University.

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:33.250
Henmi Takehiko?

00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:36.200
Yes, sir. He indicated that he wishes to speak with you about studying abroad.

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:39.560
Studying abroad? Henmi-kun?

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:42.190
Is he an aquaintance of yours, sir?

00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:46.460
Oh.... Yes, I know him well.

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:48.530
So, then... about his appointment...?

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:54.250
How 'bout a beer?

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:55.530
Nah, I'm fine.

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:59.650
What a surprise! You, turning down a beer?

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:02.740
Even I have times when I just don't feel like drinking.

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:11.450
It was so sudden, wasn't it.... About Rei-san....

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:15.010
She was an amazing person.

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:23.680
Come on. I think I'll have one after all.

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:26.220
OK.

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:43.580
Father... Fukiko... the whole family.... Everyone is obsessed over it.

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:47.320
Absolutely obsessed.

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:50.650
You know why?

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:51.920
Hmm?

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:55.470
Because we never did a <i>thing</i> for that girl in her life!

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:58.820
And now the regret over that is coming back to haunt us!

00:08:58.820 --> 00:09:00.830
Call it acknowledgement of our sins, if you like.

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:07.060
She was our own child, even if she was born into an unfortunate life; yet we never lifted a finger to help her!

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:09.180
Ichinomiya!

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:13.060
Now that she has been taken away from us so early...

00:09:13.060 --> 00:09:16.480
...we realize just how many things there were that we should have done for her, but didn't!

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:18.220
As her brother... as her family...!

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:21.320
Damn it....

00:09:22.850 --> 00:09:24.260
Ichinomiya....

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:26.390
And you...!

00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:28.050
What...?

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:31.300
Don't you ever leave something undone that you'll regret later!

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:34.610
Leave no regrets....

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:38.550
Like Nanako?

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:40.530
You idiot!

00:09:40.530 --> 00:09:42.740
Don't play dumb with me! You know who I'm talking about!

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:47.170
If she were to go, too, no words of yours could ever make me forgive you!

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:50.180
I know.

00:09:50.180 --> 00:09:51.450
Do you really?

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:54.400
Then why?! What's with this "study abroad" business?!

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:57.220
I'm giving that serious thought as well....

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:06.640
Nanako-san, telephone!

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:09.120
Someone from the Seiran basketball club.

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:10.790
Basketball club...?

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:14.160
Yes?

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:15.160
<i>Misonoo speaking....</i>

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:19.190
What? Kaoru-no-Kimi...?

00:10:19.190 --> 00:10:21.670
Yes, and we're in a pinch here.

00:10:21.670 --> 00:10:24.820
We have a match starting at six, and she hasn't shown up yet.

00:10:26.710 --> 00:10:28.850
No one at her home knows anything, either.

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:30.530
They say she hasn't come home since yesterday!

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:36.630
<i>My dear brother... Kaoru-no-Kimi...!</i>

00:10:57.890 --> 00:11:00.900
I'm tired, Rei. So tired....

00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:22.440
What's wrong?

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:24.450
What are you doing in a place like this?

00:11:27.090 --> 00:11:28.640
Ichinomiya-san!

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:29.840
What's happened?

00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:34.790
I was stopping by to visit Saint-Juste-sama's room....

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:40.480
I must seem like an idiot, I know....

00:11:41.180 --> 00:11:44.800
It's not Saint-Juste-sama's room any more....

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:48.820
I should have known that someone else would be living there now, but....

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:53.280
Saint-Juste-sama would know...

00:11:53.280 --> 00:11:58.440
I thought that if something had happened to Kaoru-no-Kimi, Saint-Juste-sama would know.

00:11:59.620 --> 00:12:03.570
The elevator had already reached the fifth floor; I was just about to ring the bell...

00:12:04.980 --> 00:12:10.750
...and then it finally occured to me that she wasn't there any more...

00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:19.050
Nanako-san, what's happened?

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:21.130
What's this about Orihara-kun?

00:12:21.650 --> 00:12:25.340
She didn't show up for a basketball match.

00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:27.350
They say she hasn't been home since last night.

00:12:28.340 --> 00:12:29.550
Is that true?

00:12:29.550 --> 00:12:30.890
Yes.

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:33.300
Get in! Get in the car!

00:12:33.300 --> 00:12:33.970
What...?

00:12:33.970 --> 00:12:35.840
Come on, hurry...

00:12:38.810 --> 00:12:40.210
Um...?

00:12:40.210 --> 00:12:41.960
We're going to Henmi's place.

00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:44.990
I want you to talk to him, OK?

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:47.740
About Orihara-kun. About her condition, in particular.

00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:52.080
What? To my brother? About Kaoru-no-Kimi...?

00:12:52.740 --> 00:12:55.960
Yes. Anything you know.

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:59.580
Why? Why would Henmi-san want to know about Kaoru-no-Kimi?

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:03.880
So... you never knew, Nanako-san?

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:07.830
Henmi Takehiko is the one person she needs more than anyone right now.

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:16.050
About a year or so ago, those two were a couple.

00:13:17.990 --> 00:13:19.740
For certain reasons, they broke up.

00:13:21.040 --> 00:13:24.860
But even so, it isn't as though they hate or even dislike one another.

00:13:25.630 --> 00:13:29.050
Even now, they share a bond in their hearts.

00:13:29.050 --> 00:13:31.060
That's how it seems to me, anyway.

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:37.320
<i>My dear brother...</i>

00:13:37.320 --> 00:13:39.660
<i>...I never knew...</i>

00:14:00.170 --> 00:14:02.180
<i>Because I love you, I must leave you.</i>

00:14:03.430 --> 00:14:05.440
<i>Because I love you, I must forget you.</i>

00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:10.200
<i>I must even make myself forget that there was ever anything to forget...</i>

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:15.440
<i>All that, because I love you so!</i>

00:14:30.310 --> 00:14:31.520
Rei...

00:14:31.520 --> 00:14:35.610
Why did you have to die while I lived on?

00:14:36.410 --> 00:14:39.420
I thought that I would go on living...

00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:45.720
I thought that I would do my best to go on living with what little time I have left, but...

00:14:46.420 --> 00:14:50.040
You never troubled anyone; you always kept to yourself...

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:54.060
You lived your life without regrets. So beautiful... so pure...

00:14:54.850 --> 00:14:58.530
Ah, Rei! To think that you would die before me...

00:14:58.530 --> 00:15:01.080
Did your courage never falter?

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:03.420
Weren't you ever afraid of dying?

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:08.940
When you felt lonely, so very lonely...

00:15:08.940 --> 00:15:12.090
...did you ever find yourself not knowing what to do...?

00:15:20.160 --> 00:15:23.840
Everyone has been coping as best they could.

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:28.330
No one realized just how much of a shock Rei's death was to her.

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:36.540
Henmi...

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:38.620
Would you lend me the car keys?

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:39.760
Yes, of course.

00:15:55.410 --> 00:15:57.690
<i>My brother, the love between you and Kaoru-no-Kimi...</i>

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:03.070
<i>Takashi-san said that it came to an end over a year ago...</i>

00:16:03.610 --> 00:16:06.890
<i>He said that you had parted ways, though you were still bound to one another in your hearts.</i>

00:16:07.510 --> 00:16:10.330
<i>He wouldn't tell me the reason why.</i>

00:16:10.990 --> 00:16:14.470
<i>But... it must have been a sorrowful romance.</i>

00:16:14.470 --> 00:16:17.020
<i>So I thought.</i>

00:16:19.530 --> 00:16:23.880
<i>Mightn't Kaoru-no-Kimi have experienced such a love long ago?</i>

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:25.760
<i>I'd had a feeling that that might have been the case.</i>

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:28.330
Welcome back, Nanako.

00:16:28.330 --> 00:16:30.740
Oh, did you borrow an umbrella from someone?

00:16:30.740 --> 00:16:33.760
What? Oh, yes. From my brother.

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:36.690
<i>But, my dear brother...</i>

00:16:36.690 --> 00:16:40.310
<i>My silent, strong, kind brother...</i>

00:16:42.590 --> 00:16:45.330
<i>Henmi... Takehiko....</i>

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:52.640
<i>The fact that that's a person's name, a man's name, has suddenly been made a little more real to me.</i>

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:17.380
I figured that you had to be here.

00:17:17.950 --> 00:17:19.490
Stay away!

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:30.360
I knew this was where you had to be!

00:17:31.600 --> 00:17:34.350
Go away! Don't trouble yourself over me!

00:17:36.250 --> 00:17:39.600
I've been waiting this past year, waiting the whole time...

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:41.680
Waiting until you needed me...

00:17:41.680 --> 00:17:44.430
I told you before, I'll live my life alone!

00:17:44.430 --> 00:17:46.770
That's not true! It's not true!

00:17:46.770 --> 00:17:48.180
Let me go!

00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:50.190
Let me go, Takehiko-san!

00:17:53.560 --> 00:17:55.710
Then why did you come to this place?

00:17:55.710 --> 00:17:58.320
Why did you come here, to the place where we parted for the last time?

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:03.250
Ever since then, ever since that time when we parted here...

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:05.930
...my heart has remained here, at this place!

00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:10.020
That part of me that said "I love you" has lingered on, here, in this place!

00:18:11.660 --> 00:18:14.940
And you, too... Your heart...

00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:17.150
It was left behind here, as well!

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:19.630
You're wrong. I have forgotten.

00:18:19.630 --> 00:18:22.040
I have forgotten all about those sorts of things.

00:18:23.730 --> 00:18:26.550
I love you! I love you!!

00:18:27.920 --> 00:18:30.470
So look at me. I want you to see...

00:18:31.100 --> 00:18:34.780
Because I want you to forget me, I want you to see...

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:46.560
You see? I could never bring you happiness.

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:51.220
Even if you could love me the way I am...

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:53.700
...the more we felt for one another...

00:18:53.700 --> 00:18:57.320
...the bleaker your future would become, because of me.

00:18:57.320 --> 00:19:02.150
And so... and so... I must forget you now...

00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:09.210
Please, tell me that you need me now!

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:17.900
Kaoru...

00:19:29.290 --> 00:19:33.570
All of the wonderful times that we had were precious moments for me.

00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:35.110
Thank you...

00:19:37.190 --> 00:19:38.330
Kaoru!

00:19:41.380 --> 00:19:42.380
KAORU!!!

00:19:58.730 --> 00:20:00.880
<i>The rain let up before dawn.</i>

00:20:05.650 --> 00:20:08.930
Ah! Sorry to trouble you, but is this the Orihara residence?

00:20:12.800 --> 00:20:15.340
Nanako-san, what about breakfast? Won't you be having something?

00:20:16.140 --> 00:20:18.690
Ah! Yes, I'll be right back.

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:21.300
Be right back...? Where are you off to so early?

00:20:21.840 --> 00:20:23.640
They said that she's returned!

00:20:23.650 --> 00:20:24.380
What?

00:20:24.380 --> 00:20:26.530
Who has? Where?

00:20:26.530 --> 00:20:28.540
The folks at her home told me.

00:20:28.540 --> 00:20:30.950
She came back late last night!

00:20:31.420 --> 00:20:33.030
What's she talking about?

00:20:33.030 --> 00:20:34.100
No idea...

00:20:34.100 --> 00:20:39.060
Not only that, but she's headed off to the morning basketball practice, up at the school!

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:40.870
I'm off!

00:20:40.870 --> 00:20:42.010
Nanako-san...?!

00:20:58.430 --> 00:21:00.980
It wasn't true - there was no early morning practice...

00:21:12.560 --> 00:21:15.100
<i>"I wish that Saint-Juste-sama were here..."</i>

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:18.730
<i>Perhaps that's what I was saying to myself...</i>

00:21:30.300 --> 00:21:31.570
Yo.

00:21:32.860 --> 00:21:34.330
This place...

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:38.550
I guess you remembered that it was Rei's favorite place.

00:21:40.660 --> 00:21:42.810
She used to skip class here all the time.

00:21:45.360 --> 00:21:48.240
You know... everyone has been worried about you!

00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:50.720
The basketball club... Ichinomiya-san...

00:21:50.720 --> 00:21:52.590
...and Henmi-san, too!

00:21:52.590 --> 00:21:56.410
Oh, yeah... I'd totally forgotten about the game...

00:21:56.410 --> 00:21:59.220
Um... I heard from Ichinomiya-san...

00:21:59.230 --> 00:22:01.100
...about Henmi-san...

00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:05.340
That's all over now, but... would you like to know?

00:22:05.340 --> 00:22:06.550
Ah... eh...?!

00:22:09.860 --> 00:22:12.610
Back when Rei and I had first become friends...

00:22:12.610 --> 00:22:15.690
...Ichinomiya-san came over to Rei's place.

00:22:15.690 --> 00:22:18.780
Ichinomiya-san introduced Henmi-san to me.

00:22:19.500 --> 00:22:22.250
I fell in love the moment we met.

00:22:22.250 --> 00:22:25.260
Those dark brown eyes sparkled so enchantingly...

00:22:28.770 --> 00:22:30.710
We went various places...

00:22:32.220 --> 00:22:35.640
Yeah... one time the two of us rode the carousel together...

00:22:38.930 --> 00:22:41.340
It made for a splendid memory...

00:22:48.540 --> 00:22:50.950
But... we broke up.

00:22:56.050 --> 00:22:59.740
I wonder whether you should know the reason why...

00:22:59.740 --> 00:23:00.470
Eh...?!

00:23:12.800 --> 00:23:16.880
The surgery, you see. They had to remove one.

00:23:28.530 --> 00:23:30.070
Five years...

00:23:30.070 --> 00:23:33.820
When a relapse occurs within five years... there isn't really any hope...

00:23:48.900 --> 00:23:50.380
<i>Kaoru...</i>

00:24:10.160 --> 00:24:14.360
I dreamed I was chasing a rainbow...

00:24:14.360 --> 00:24:19.830
Then the rainbow I was chasing was you.

00:24:21.300 --> 00:24:25.440
Before, I had no strength, no will.

00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:30.910
But now because of you, I do.

00:24:31.650 --> 00:24:37.190
Feelings of love, like raindrops

00:24:37.190 --> 00:24:42.660
Come pouring from the sky.

00:24:42.660 --> 00:24:45.390
This is surely a game

00:24:45.390 --> 00:24:48.200
Of some mischievous fairy...

00:24:48.200 --> 00:24:50.600
Always dancing,

00:24:50.600 --> 00:24:55.870
Always capricious...

00:25:02.020 --> 00:25:05.430
In the next episode...

00:25:05.900 --> 00:25:10.770
Nanako knows that Henmi is her true brother.

00:25:10.780 --> 00:25:17.010
Henmi and Misonoo meet again after more than ten years to reaffirm the love of a parent and a child.

00:25:17.010 --> 00:25:22.270
So begins their journey forth into a new day... and...

00:25:23.080 --> 00:25:25.490
Next time: <b>Merry-Go-Round</b>

00:25:26.080 --> 00:25:31.110
My dear brother... there is no end to my tears...
